lf-contract 0.1
# The clamp contract of the plan draft's §7.4, for scripts/program_vc.py.
id lf-clamp/0
word lf-clamp
ir tests/program/ir/clamp.ir
stack ( value lower upper -- result true | false )
inputs value lower upper
statement For integers v, l, u in the cell range: if l ≤ u the word returns r = min(max(v, l), u) and true, so l ≤ r ≤ u, r = v when l ≤ v ≤ u, r = l when v < l and r = u when v > u; if l > u it consumes its three inputs and returns false. Cells below are kept.
case lower > upper
  out false
case lower <= upper
  out r true
  ensure r = min(max(value, lower), upper)
  ensure lower <= r && r <= upper
  ensure lower <= value && value <= upper -> r = value
  ensure value < lower -> r = lower
  ensure value > upper -> r = upper
expect discharged
